{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>You may charge interest to the foreigner.</b> You may give him interest if you have stipulated it with him, and you shall not deal falsely." "<b>But to your brother you shall not charge interest.</b> Even though you stipulated it with him and you are willing to pay it, it is forbidden for you to give him interest." "<b>In order that He may bless you.</b> When you do not deal falsely with the foreigner and do not profane the Name."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:22:02.021822429Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}